    "kind": "behavior",
    "description": "Operational proxy diagnosis now distinguishes client cancellation, deadlines, refused local daemon, reset, EOF and timeout using fixed safe categories and numeric request latency; installation and repair scope stay unchanged.",
    "implementation": "Inspected web/src/bridge.ts bounded known-read retries and rejected-handshake replacement, Factory poll/action separation, ItemDetail/Agent local read recovery, plus gateway proxyError fixed-class logging and audit numeric duration. Start/Send/answers/saves are never automatically retried, and no auth material enters the iframe or logs.",
    "tests": "Read six UI-CONNECT browser cases: three failed initial handshakes then recovery; polling outage and draft preservation; item read recovery with one displayed-revision read; transcript retention; uncertain Send once with surviving error; and tool-result Connection failed text not retried. Gateway tests classify seven failure categories, exclude hidden request/error values and preserve 502/streaming; audit tests assert nonnegative numeric latency and no request details. Existing flow assertions and stable manual/host gaps remain."
